EXPERIMENT 14 – AUTOMATING CHECKBOX AND RADIO BUTTON SELECTION USING SELENIUM

AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to automate checkbox and radio button selection.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the Selenium 4 dependency.
2. Open the checkboxes page and collect all checkboxes using findElements().
3. Check the initial state using isSelected().
4. Select the first checkbox and clear the second checkbox using click().
5. Open the web form page and select the second radio button.
6. Print the selection states and close the browser.
CODE
Exercise14.java
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import java.util.List;

public class Exercise14 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();

            driver.get("https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/checkboxes");

            List<WebElement> boxes = driver.findElements(
                By.cssSelector("input[type='checkbox']")
            );

            System.out.println("Checkbox 1 initially selected : "
                + boxes.get(0).isSelected());

            System.out.println("Checkbox 2 initially selected : "
                + boxes.get(1).isSelected());

            if (!boxes.get(0).isSelected())
                boxes.get(0).click();

            if (boxes.get(1).isSelected())
                boxes.get(1).click();

            System.out.println("Checkbox 1 after click : "
                + boxes.get(0).isSelected());

            System.out.println("Checkbox 2 after click : "
                + boxes.get(1).isSelected());

            driver.get("https://www.selenium.dev/selenium/web/web-form.html");

            driver.findElement(By.id("my-radio-2")).click();

            System.out.println("Radio 1 selected : "
                + driver.findElement(By.id("my-radio-1")).isSelected());

            System.out.println("Radio 2 selected : "
                + driver.findElement(By.id("my-radio-2")).isSelected());

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
- Checkbox 1: Initially unchecked
- Checkbox 2: Initially checked
- Radio button: Select the second option
OUTPUT
Checkbox 1 initially selected : false
Checkbox 2 initially selected : true
Checkbox 1 after click : true
Checkbox 2 after click : false
Radio 1 selected : false
Radio 2 selected : true


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to automate checkbox and radio button selection was executed successfully and the output was verified.
